      cells: "IKIIII",
      note: "CAISO KEEPER (caiso-139, OWNER PROMOTION 2026-07-29 — A/B passes every pre-registered gate, chartered from the caiso-138 §B beta filing). Arms 2026-07-29-caiso139-control / -dump-guard-offer, same pushed HEAD, control byte-identical to the caiso-138 keeper. P1 dump 0.5218 -> 0.0000 TWh / 175 -> 0 h (DSW 2024) and 0.0088/0.0141/0.0208 -> 0.0000 on the other three node-years, EXACT. P2 E1/E2 = +0.0000 all three years with max CA per-zone-hour |dprice| = 0.0000 (CA-side LP byte-identical, as the D3 reduced-cost argument required). P3 rubric IDENTICAL: NOT-YET, fail {C3a, C3c}. P4 2023 null control byte-identical across ALL zones (the guard is unchanged in 2023 — a built-in control). P5 is the structural confirmation and not a degenerate corner: the node now clears at lambda = measured hub + OATT wheel + eps — the marginal DELIVERED import offer — verified to 0.0000, max |delta| 0.0000, in 100.0% of all 212 former dump hours (wheel $4.00 DSW / $5.00 PNW from CAISO_IMPORT_DELIVERY_BASIS). build_cost_vector's dump price exists so no row can profit by generating purely to dump, but its minimum ran over (wind_mc, solar_mc, -storage_eac) ONLY — every other negative offer slipped under it. CAISO's per-hub import tranches carry their own measured hub, and Palo Verde crashes to -$58.24/MWh (2024) / -$36.26 (2025), so DSW_surplus_clean & co. booked $3.69-32.24/MWh of pure generate-to-dump: 0.531 TWh (2024) and 0.035 TWh (2025) of phantom tranche revenue printing the WECC nodes at the -$26.001 dump optimum. Fix = the SAME guard over its full domain (rule 19), min additionally spanning every mc row with pmax > 0; export sinks (pmax 0, pmin -cap) stay outside because their negative price is a willingness-to-pay on a WITHDRAWAL, and they sit BELOW the producible min (2024: -58.2407 vs -58.2387), so dropping the mask would inflate the guard. Zero new DOF (rule 24) — read off the LP's own offer arrays per solve. The alternative repair (floor the import offers at -dump_cost, the virtual_bids._inc_offer_floor treatment) is REFUSED under rule 14: on this corpus it would actively rewrite measured hub prices (-58.24 -> -26.00), not stay the structural no-op it is for the PJM virtuals. Cross-ISO census on every keeper's own fleet, all three years (probe §E): ERCOT -2.84/+1.40/+1.40, MISO/NEISO/NYISO/PJM +1.40 — no non-CAISO keeper is within $24/MWh of the guard, so the repair is CAISO-only IN EFFECT and each of those cells is measured-inert ex ante (I), not transferred. PJM's virtual layer is settled analytically and more strongly: DEC rows are pmax 0 (outside the mask by construction) and INC rungs are ALREADY floored at min_credit + eps >= -dump_cost + eps by _inc_offer_floor — the same invariant, enforced there on the offer side. Ships flag-gated default-off despite being an LP soundness invariant, because dump_cost is ISO-agnostic infrastructure (rule 25: each lane arms it on its own evidence) and the gate keeps every pre-existing cache key byte-stable.",
