      cells: ".UKGGU",
      note: "PJM keeper — moved 2025 C3c 0→17h and fixed C1/C3a/C3b/C7. MISO REFUSED ex ante, NO SOLVE SPENT (miso-105) — and refused on the OPPOSITE evidence from NYISO's: MISO DOES publish the submitted priced curve, so the mechanism was measured on its own complete book instead of being blocked at identification. SOURCE FOUND (new for the repo): MISO's FERC-Order-719 masked demand-bid archive docs.misoenergy.org/marketreports/YYYYMMDD_bids_cb.zip, ~90-day lag, one row per bid×hour with PRICE1..9/MW1..9 + cleared MW + LMP; rolling window is 2023-01-01→2026-01-01 and 404s on every rule-22 holdout year. LADDER SEMANTICS IDENTIFIED FROM THE FILE, not assumed: reading (PRICE_i,MW_i) as INCREMENTAL blocks and clearing them against the row's own LMP reproduces the published cleared MW for 99.36 % of 207,549 priced virtual bid-hours (MAE 0.028 MW) vs 93.49 %/0.410 cumulative — and 66.66 % of bid-hours carry submitted blocks that did NOT clear, so it is the submitted curve. PROVENANCE PROVED IN BOTH DIRECTIONS: cleared MW = 16.3 %/14.9 % of load in 2024 vs the IMM's published 15.8 %/14.5 % (2024 SOM App. Table A2), while the submitted ladder is 2.49-2.79× larger. Refused on three measured grounds. (1) PREMISE FALSE — PJM's lever runs on +7-11 GW net DEC at the top summer hours; MISO's summer-peak net cleared virtual is +1.09/+2.47/−0.34 GW and NEGATIVE in 2025, the year C3b fails; RT>$300 tail net is −158/+1,336/−62 MW across 6/13/28 hours. MISO's book is 2.7× PJM's as a share of load GROSS (15.8/14.5 vs 5.9/5.6 %) and ≈0 NET — a convergence/congestion instrument, verbatim the IMM (2025 SOM §IV.B: 'essential to price convergence', 1,694 MW/h of energy-neutral MATCHED pairs). (2) IMMATERIAL where admissible — the peak-minus-night net differential (+1.40/+1.28/+0.43 GW) at the keeper's own re-measured summer stack slope (0.54/0.56/0.64 $/GW) buys +$0.75/+$0.72/+$0.27 of diurnal spread against a $14.6/$15.9/$20.5 C3b summer gap = 5.1/4.5/1.3 %, SHRINKING as the miss grows. (3) THE MATERIAL CHANNEL IS INADMISSIBLE (the new blocker nyiso-94 never reached, because NYISO had no data to reach it) — the curve's crossing price λ0 reproduces the price its own book cleared at to $0.09/$1.80/$0.17, and its stiffness (0.93/0.93/0.69 GW per $/MWh) against the model stack's elasticity (1.85/1.79/1.56 GW/$) means arming it supplies 31-34 % of EVERY hour's price displacement and ~63 % at the steepest 2025 summer ventile. The model's price would substantially become the measured book's crossing price — rule 1, and rule 13's forward test dies because whatever regenerates the curve forward must reproduce λ0, which IS the price the model exists to forecast. NOTE FOR PJM'S LANE (observation, NOT a verdict — rule 25): the λ0-attractor question is a property of the family and was never asked in PJM; PJM's premise is genuinely different (+7-11 GW of real depth), so it needs PJM's own λ0-gap and N÷(S+N) measurement. NYISO REFUSED ex ante, NO SOLVE SPENT (nyiso-94): PJM's lever is admissible because hrl_da_incs_decs is the SUBMITTED curve; NYISO publishes no submitted-curve equivalent at any grain. Four independent blockers. (1) NO PRICE AXIS — P-59 zonalBidLoad gives ONE MW per zone-hour for Virtual Load/Supply, so net(λ) needs an assumed price distribution = a fitted scalar (rule 21). (2) CLEARED, NOT SUBMITTED (rule 13) — the zonalBidLoad virtual columns reproduce the IMM's published CLEARED MW/h (2025 SOM Fig 24) to within 1-2 MW: 1090/1275 vs 1089/1275 (2024), 1052/1329 vs 1051/1327 (2025). The P-27 masked archive HAS prices but cannot separate virtual from physical price-capped load (corr 0.667 vs Virtual Load, 0.894 vs Price Cap Load, best 0.912 vs their SUM at 0.78x level; the 834 no-Forecast/no-Fixed 'financial-signature' sinks partition cleanly from the 1,350 physical ones yet total 2.46x published Virtual Load — a mixture, not an identification). (3) PREMISE FALSE — PJM's +7-11 GW net DEC at peak vs NYISO net virtual NEGATIVE in the mean hour (−230/−186/−277 MW) and only +580/+293/+917 MW in the measured RT>$300 tail (~1/10th PJM); NYISO's whole DA book sits 846-869 MW BELOW RT load, and the IMM says the same (2025 SOM p.47: DA net scheduled load ~96% of actual peak load). (4) ROOF-BLOCKED on the keeper's own sidecars — all five MAINLAND zones share ONE identical max dual (149.9/194.5/255.1), 0 h >$258, ZERO load-shed slack in all three years; every model >$300 hour is Long Island, where net virtual is only +211/+145/+249 MW. SUCCESSOR LEVER IDENTIFIED: NYISO's virtual market is a CONGESTION play (net DEC downstate NYC +872 / Lower_Hudson +420, net INC upstate Capital_Hudson −403 — verbatim the IMM's 'purchasing load downstate and selling virtual energy upstate', 2025 SOM p.21), and the keeper prices Lower_Hudson−Upstate_West at $0.0 in the very tail hours the IMM says TSA (Thunderstorm Alert) congestion runs $300-500/MWh. TSA cuts upstate→downstate transfer 1-2 GW, RT-ONLY, hours 13-21 May-Sep, 50 h carrying 99% of its cost — unmodelled here, and the recommended NYISO C3c lane. NEISO stays U (rule 25: derives its own; whether ISO-NE publishes a SUBMITTED curve is untested). ERCOT DAM depth handled by its own cleared-share ladder; MISO untested (see lever queue).",
