      cells: "KUUR.R",
      note: "ERCOT keeper at plant grain (ERCOT-96/97) — SINCE 2026-07-29 (ercot137 keeper, owner ruling R2) INCLUDING COAL: ercot_thermal_dam_availability_coal is ADOPTED as the ERCOT backcast default (backcast_config, ERCOT-scoped), with the water-fill restore ceiling fixed to pmax×BIN_FORCED_DERATE_BY_YEAR so a destroyed unit is never resurrected (Martin Lake 1.451→1.059; the ERCOT-135 §7.2 blocker discharged). Impossible plant-hours in the keeper: 3,846/3,462/2,622 (−83/−86/−91% vs the retired estimate). The coal fit-cost of the accurate envelope (the un-pinned over-run) is the recorded open root-cause lane on the coal-vs-gas ranking, NOT a reason to revert (rule 14). Historical text follows. COAL-SCOPE RE-GATE ON THE CURRENT KEEPER (ERCOT-134, 2026-07-28, pre-committed A/B, run 2026-07-28-ercot116-regate-arm): the measured envelope is MEASURED-CORRECT — impossible plant-hours (CAMPD actual above the model's entire available capacity) fall 22,633/24,627/30,697 -> 3,846/3,462/2,622 (-83/-86/-91%) — and REJECTED AGAIN on level: the un-pinned coal over-runs +6.5/+9.6/+11.4 TWh, G1 loading-vs-price collapses 20/21 -> 1/21 (over-loaded in every band), C3a -35.3/-14.7/-13.2%. Confirms ERCOT-116 on the ercot129 recipe + Sandy Creek repair: the estimate's carve-out is load-bearing for the fit because it silently absorbs a coal-vs-gas mid-merit ranking bias (rule 14). Owner adoption ruling still OPEN; successor = the coal-vs-gas merit-order lane on the un-pinned fleet (DIAGNOSIS-ercot134 s10), opened as ERCOT-135 Phase 1 (no-LP, 2026-07-28: the bias is a coal offer-curve SHAPE defect sized 3.2-4.2 GW). NEW INPUT TO THE ADOPTION RULING (ERCOT-135 §7.2): the plant-grain water-fill saturates each plant at its MODEL pmax — per-plant ARM/declared equals pmax/declared-max to three decimals at every plant — so it tracks the COP declaration's shape but not its level, and can lift a plant back above a forced derate modelling a physically destroyed unit. Martin Lake's 1.451 overshoot is exactly that (pmax 2,380 MW vs declared max ~1,640; unit 1 destroyed, carried by BIN_FORCED_DERATE_BY_YEAR N_COAL4 {2025: 0.67}). The envelope is therefore NOT adoptable as-is without deciding how the redistribution and the forced-derate registry compose. PJM: data intaken 2026-07-24, ships default-off — UNTESTED LEVER. CAISO built untested (caiso_dam_outages). NYISO: no equivalent disclosure (60-Day reconstruction used for bridge params instead). NEISO: operable-capacity source NOT ADOPTED (fleet-wide denominator on thermal-only application, neiso-62); MISO native outage source REVERTED on grain (miso-85/86) — its outage-grain data ask is the standing instrument-blocked lane.",
